#### Mapping STAR data-set

Previous section describes how to generate an arrival of request as well as its classification to a particular user. Next ultimate goal is to assign location of the request to a specific tape and also number of bytes that request is asking for. As one can think of, the generation of these two attributes needs to again follow a pattern that has a notion of randomness. This pattern is in reality related to a certain data-set containing many physical files which a user (or multiple users) is asking for.

